# .gitignore — agent-atlas-growth-department
#
# Owner: Repository Architect (Phase 01). Run ID phase-01-2026-07-28-a.
# Purpose: guarantee the Phase 01 pass condition "No secrets committed," and keep
# the repository clean on Windows.
#
# Fail-closed principle: when it is undecided whether a class of file may be
# tracked, exclude it now and narrow the rule later by an owner decision recorded
# in DECISIONS.md. Widening this file is a boundary change — see
# docs/PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md § "How to change a boundary".
#
# Most rules below are pre-emptive: Phase 01 produces Markdown only. Code,
# schemas, and adapters arrive in Phases 04, 13, and 16.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets — never commit, no exceptions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per user-guide/USER_INSTRUCTIONS.md: .env is for local development, .env.example
# holds placeholder variable names only, Google Secret Manager holds production
# secrets. No credential of any kind belongs in this repository.

# NOTE: Git only treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line. Every comment in
# this file is therefore on its own line — a trailing `#` would become part of
# the pattern and silently break the rule.

.env
.env.*
# .env.example is the ONLY .env-family file that is tracked: placeholder
# variable names, never real values.
!.env.example

# Private keys and certificate bundles
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# Google / OAuth credential files, by their conventional filenames. Phases 05,
# 16, 17, and 18 anticipate Google and third-party API access; none is connected
# today (docs/PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md § "External system boundaries"), so these
# rules exist before the files could.
service-account*.json
client_secret*.json
credentials.json
token.json
*-credentials.json
*_credentials.json
.gcloud/
gha-creds-*.json

# Catch-all secret directories
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Harness / machine-local configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per D-032. .claude/settings.local.json records per-machine Claude Code
# permission allowances. It is harness configuration, not project work — in Phase
# 00 a subagent wrote it outside its assigned scope and it had to be disclosed in
# the gate report (findings.md F-00-09). Ignore that one file only.
#
# Do NOT ignore all of .claude/ — project-level agent configuration that later
# phases may add belongs under version control.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Local data that must never sync
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per D-033. Q-009 (data-privacy handling for lead/contact data) is UNRESOLVED — no
# retention, storage, or deletion rules exist. Because the answer is unknown,
# this project fails closed and excludes any private data directory PRE-EMPTIVELY,
# before Phase 04 defines a lead schema and before Phase 17 could collect
# anything. This exclusion is not a substitute for the missing policy: no
# lead, contact, or personal data may be collected or stored at all until Q-009
# is resolved (docs/PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md § "Data boundaries").
data/private/
data/leads/
data/contacts/
*.leads.csv
*.contacts.csv


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Archives — deliberately NOT blanket-ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is intentionally no `*.zip` rule in this file.
# agent-atlas-growth-department_build-package_draft.zip is the provenance
# artifact for the entire build package and MUST stay tracked so the original
# package is recoverable. Decided by the Phase 01 Owner and recorded as D-031.
# If a future phase needs to exclude generated archives, exclude them by specific
# path or directory — do not add a blanket `*.zip`.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Windows / OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
# Windows shortcuts embed machine-specific absolute paths.
*.lnk
*.stackdump
# macOS cruft, in case the repository is ever cloned there.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Editors and IDEs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VS Code / Antigravity: exclude machine-local workspace state, keep the shared
# extension recommendation list so a new clone gets the same tooling prompt.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# JetBrains project state.
.idea/
*.iml
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
# vim swap/backup files.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# VS Code "Local History" extension — snapshots of every save, including of files
# that may hold secrets before they are cleaned up.
.history/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Runtime, dependencies, and build output (pre-emptive)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node — Phase 16 adds src/adapters/; publishing adapters are the first source code.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.nuxt/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnp.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Terraform / infra state — state files routinely contain secrets in plain text
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Logs, temporary and scratch files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The phase checklist requires temporary files to be kept separate from
# deliverables. Throwaway work belongs in the OS temp/scratchpad location, not
# in the repository — these rules are the backstop, not the policy.
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pip-log.txt
tmp/
temp/
.tmp/
scratch/
scratchpad/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Not ignored, stated explicitly so nobody adds a rule later
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked on purpose:
#   - agent-atlas-growth-department_build-package_draft.zip  (provenance artifact)
#   - .env.example                                           (placeholder names only)
#   - agent_runs/                                            (phase evidence and handoffs — the audit trail)
#   - .claude/ except settings.local.json                    (project agent config)
#   - all governance Markdown at the repository root
